    All other files, copyright Brendan McKay (Australian National
    University, Brendan.McKay@anu.edu.au).

  nauty 2.9.3 — https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/nauty/
    A. All files not listed as B-G below, copyright Brendan McKay (1984-)
    B. Files traces.h, traces.c and dretodot.c, copyright Adolfo Piperno (2008-)
    C. File watercluster2.c and genposetg.c, copyright Gunnar Brinkmann (2009-)
    D. Files planarity.h and planarity.c, copyright Magma project.
    E. Files nautycliquer.h and nautycliquer.c, copyright to Sampo
       Niskanen and Patric Östergård.
    F. Much of file nauchromatic.c, copyright Gordon Royle.
    G. The code in nausha.c was put into the public domain by Brad Conte.

Changes made to those works: none to the sources. They are downloaded from
upstream, checksum-verified and compiled unmodified by build/build-wasm.sh,
which passes the flags of surge's own Makefile with `-march=native` removed
(a native instruction set has no meaning for a WebAssembly target). The
compiled result is stored, gzipped and base64-encoded, in src/wasm/data.ts.

